{
  "color": {
    "$type": "color",
    "$description": "The semantic colour layer for the light theme.\n\nSemantic colour lives in the theme files rather than in semantic/, because every semantic colour is theme-dependent by definition — there is no theme-neutral value for `color.canvas`. Splitting it into a semantic file plus per-theme overrides would mean writing each name twice and inventing precedence rules. Instead each theme states the whole colour contract once. The token build enforces that every theme defines exactly the same set of names, so the two files cannot drift.",
